          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சட்டம் — caṭṭam — \"a law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அரசு ஒரு புதிய சட்டம் கொண்டுவந்தது. aracu oru putiya caṭṭam koṇṭuvantatu. The government brought in a new law."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: சட்டங்கள், caṭṭaṅkaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சட்டப்படி, by law. A -அம் noun makes its plural in -ங்கள்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சட்டம் (caṭṭam) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2304 lists Tamil caṭṭam, \"wooden frame; plan, model, rule, order, regulation\": a frame that holds things in place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
